# PRODUCTION API URL — baked into the packaged app when you run `npm run build`
# (which is what `npx cap sync` bundles into the Android/iOS app).
#
# IMPORTANT: a store-downloaded app CANNOT talk to http://localhost — on a phone
# that means the phone itself. You MUST deploy the NestJS backend to a public
# HTTPS URL and put it here. Vite loads this file for production builds and it
# overrides .env.local, so `npm run dev` still uses localhost.
#
# Free hosting that works: Render / Railway / Fly.io (API) + Neon / Supabase (DB).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-DEPLOYED-API.example.com/api
